          %h2#Definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+category"} strict category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            is called
            %strong skeletal
            if any two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            that are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
            are actually already
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality"} equal
            (in the fixed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Obj
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Obj(\mathcal{C})
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
            are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphisms"} automorphisms
          %p
            (If in addition all isomorphisms are in fact
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphisms"} identity morphisms
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gaunt+category"} gaunt category
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skeletal+groupoid"} skeletal groupoid
          %p
            A
            %strong skeleton
            of a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is defined to be a skeletal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inclusion+functor"} inclusion functor
            exhibits it as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %strong weak skeleton
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is any skeletal category which is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} weakly equivalent
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            In the absence of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            %strong skeleton
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            to be a weak skeleton as defined above.
          %h2#constructions Constructions
          %p
            In this section, we work in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set-level+foundations"} set-level foundations
            to construct skeleta of categories and more general objects.
          %h3#existence_of_skeletons_of_categories Existence of Skeletons of Categories
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              If the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
              holds, then every category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              has a skeleton (in the strongest sense).
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p Simply choose one object in each isomorphism class and one isomorphism to that object from each other object in that class.
            %p
              In more detail, generate the full subcategory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sk
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sk(C)
              containing just the chosen objects. Denote by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi in
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi sk
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} in\colon sk(C)\to C
              the inclusion. We exhibit a weak inverse of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi in
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} in
              as a functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ′
                    %mo :
                    %mi x
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi x
                    %mo ′
